Flatten the Rust AST into an id-based arena

Replace the pointer-based AST with a `Vec<(Location, NodeData)>` arena in
`Ast`. Each AST node kind gets a typed id (e.g. `TermId`, `IfAtomId`) that
wraps a `NodeId`, and accessors like `ast.term(id)` panic on a variant
mismatch. Child references are stored as ids, which lets downstream passes
key maps by id without worrying about borrow lifetimes or moves.

The grammar now takes `&mut Ast` and pushes nodes into the arena as it
parses; `populate_eqlog` takes `&Ast` and a `ModuleId` and walks the arena
by id.
